      "The four original benchmark bots never built a coordinated push (about 0.17 crowns per match against each other), so win rate against them measured defence only. I added a fifth bot, PushBot, that banks elixir, commits a tank and follows with support, and kept the original four byte-for-byte unchanged so per-opponent history stays comparable.",
      "One scalar advantage for both action heads made every card update carry the noise of a 144-way placement draw. I added an optional intermediate value head V(s, card) with a separate PPO clip per head. The clean telescoping split (A_card + A_cell = A_total) starved the card head on a synthetic bandit, so the mode that ships is per-head baselines — and at 24 seeds the apparent gain in mean score shrank to noise; only a halving of seed-to-seed spread survived. The flag defaults off, with the harness and the retraction documented.",
